<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pliny the Younger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">61–c. 113</span> · Also known as Gaius Plinius Caecilius Secundus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pliny the Younger was a Roman lawyer, senator and author, nephew and adopted son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pliny-the-elder">Pliny the Elder</a>. His published letters describe Roman public and private life, including the eruption of Vesuvius in 79 CE. As governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bithynia">Bithynia</a> and Pontus around 110–112 he corresponded with the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a> on local finances and building projects and on the treatment of Christians.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pliny-the-younger.jpg" alt="Pliny the Younger" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Angelica Kauffmann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pliny_the_Younger_and_his_Mother_at_Misenum,_79_A.D.,_by_Angelica_Kauffmann,_English,_1785,_oil_on_canvas_-_Princeton_University_Art_Museum_-_DSC06494_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
